              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+string"} relativistic string
            is called the relativistic
            = succeed "." do
              %em membrane
          %p
            The concept of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic
            membrane was considered already by
            %a{:href => "#Dirac62"} Dirac 62
            as a hypothetical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            %a{:href => "#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87"} Bergshoeff-Sezgin-Townsend 87
            (whose “m” became the “M” in “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"}> M-theory
            ”), namely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model+for+super+p-branes"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model for super p-branes
            corresponding to the
            = succeed "-entry" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p=2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mn 11
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
          %p
            In fact, according to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super 2-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
            exists on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetimes"} superspacetimes
            of dimension 4, 5, 7, and 11:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                4:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-brane+in+4d"} super 2-brane in 4d
            %li
              %p
                5:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-brane+in+5d"} super 2-brane in 5d
            %li
              %p 7: …
            %li
              %p
                11:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              ´
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+instanton"} membrane instanton
          %h2#references References
          %h3#prehistory Pre-history
          %p
            Early speculations trying to unify the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/muon"} muon
            as two excitations of a single relativistic membrane:
          %ul
            %li#Dirac62
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Extensible Model of the Electron
                %strong 268
                (1962) 57-67 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2414316"}> jstor:2414316
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (also proposing the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac-Born-Infeld+action"} Dirac-Born-Infeld action
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The motion of an Extended Particle in the Gravitational Field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leopold+Infeld"} L. Infeld
                (ed.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Relativistic Theories of Gravitation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1623740"} spire:1623740
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Dirac-MotionOfAnExtendedParticle.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/2282975/files/warsaw-1962.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Dirac"}> Paul Dirac
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Particles of Finite Size in the Gravitational Field
                %strong 270
                (1962) 354-356 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1962.0228"}> doi:10.1098/rspa.1962.0228
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %div
            %h3#SuperMembraneAsSigmaModelReferences Super-membrane/M2-brane as a sigma model
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-type" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-membrane"} super-membrane
              in 11d (as in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
              and in contrast to the
              = succeed "-solutions" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            %ul
              %li#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermembranes and eleven-dimensional supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/248230/"} spire:248230
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              of the super membrane are derived via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superembedding+approach"} superembedding approach
              in
            %ul
              %li#BPSTV95
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Pasti"} Paolo Pasti
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"} Dmitri Sorokin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Tonin"} Mario Tonin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Volkov"} Dmitry Volkov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superstrings and supermembranes in the doubly supersymmetric geometrical approach
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501113"} arXiv:hep-th/9501113
            %p
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              for the super membrane is derived via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superembedding+approach"} superembedding approach
              in
            %ul
              %li#HoweSezgin05
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The supermembrane revisited
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412245"} arXiv:hep-th/0412245
            %p
              Discussion from the point of view of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
              is in
            %ul
              %li#FSS2013
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
                (2013)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
              of the M2-brane to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
              was observed in
            %ul
              %li#DuffHoweInamiStelle87
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Superstrings in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 10
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                    from Supermembranes in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo =
                          %mn 11
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"} Michael Duff
                (ed.)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
                205-206 (1987) (
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/245249"}> spire
                )
            %p
              The interpretation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-membrane"} super-membrane
              as an object related to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              via
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
              was proposed in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"}> Paul Townsend
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The eleven-dimensional supermembrane revisited
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501068"} arXiv:hep-th/9501068
            %p
              around the time when
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              became accepted due to
            %ul
              %li#Witten95
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"}> arXiv:hep-th/9503124
                )
            %p See also
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The supermembrane revisited
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412245"} arXiv:hep-th/0412245
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                  %em SDiff Gauge Theory and the M2 Condensate
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1583"}> arXiv:0808.1583
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  M.P. Garcia del Moral, C. Las Heras, P. Leon, J.M. Pena, A. Restuccia,
                  %em
                    Fluxes, Twisted tori, Monodromy and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                    Supermembranes
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.06397"}> arXiv:2005.06397
                  )
          %div
            %h3#LightConeQuantizationOfM2BranesToBFSSMatrixModel Quantization of the M2-brane sigma-model to a matrix model
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-formulation" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge"} light-cone gauge
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
              for the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+membrane"} relativistic membrane
              and the corresponding matrix
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutator"} commutator
              regularization is due to:
            %ul
              %li#Hoppe82
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum theory of a massless relativistic surface and a two-dimensional bound state problem
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1721.1/15717"} dspace:1721.1/15717
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HoppeMembrane82.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p Some exact solutions:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em Exact algebraic M(em)brane solutions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.00569"} arXiv:2107.00569
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em The fast non-commutative sharp drop
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.13146"} arXiv:2302.13146
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              On the regularized
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge+quantization"} light-cone gauge quantization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
              on (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"}> super
              )
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
            %p Original articles:
            %ul
              %li#deWitHoppeNicolai88
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernard+de+Wit"}> Bernard de Wit
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"} Jens Hoppe
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Quantum Mechanics of Supermembranes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://pubman.mpdl.mpg.de/pubman/item/escidoc:153408:1/component/escidoc:153407/353961.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/deWitHoppeNicolai88.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/261702"} spire:261702
            %p Observation that the spectrum is continuous:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernard+de+Wit"}> Bernard de Wit
                , W. Lüscher,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The supermembrane is unstable
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/266584/"} spire:266584
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(89)90214-9"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(89)90214-9
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li#NicolaiHelling98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"}> Hermann Nicolai
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+C.+Helling"} Robert C. Helling
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supermembranes and M(atrix) Theory
                  %em Trieste 1998, Nonperturbative aspects of strings, branes and supersymmetry
                  29-74 (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9809103"}> arXiv:hep-th/9809103
                  ,
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/476366"} spire:476366
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em Membranes and Matrix Models
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0206192"}> arXiv:hep-th/0206192
                  )
              %li#DasguptaNicolaiPlefka02
                %p
                  Arundhati Dasgupta,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Nicolai"} Hermann Nicolai
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Plefka"} Jan Plefka
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em An Introduction to the Quantum Supermembrane
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201182"} arXiv:hep-th/0201182
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+van+den+Oord"}> Gijs van den Oord
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On Matrix Regularisation of Supermembranes
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://web.science.uu.nl/itf/Teaching/2006/vandenOord.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meer+Ashwinkumar"}> Meer Ashwinkumar
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lennart+Schmidt"} Lennart Schmidt
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meng-Chwan+Tan"} Meng-Chwan Tan
                  %em
                    Matrix Regularization of Classical Nambu Brackets and Super
                    = succeed "-Branes" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.06666"}> arXiv:2103.06666
                  )
            %p
              The generalization to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pp-wave+spacetimes"} pp-wave spacetimes
              (leading to the
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
            %ul
              %li#DSJVR02
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keshav+Dasgupta"}> Keshav Dasgupta
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mohammad+Sheikh-Jabbari"} Mohammad Sheikh-Jabbari
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Van+Raamsdonk"} Mark Van Raamsdonk
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Matrix Perturbation Theory For M-theory On a PP-Wave
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205185"} arXiv:hep-th/0205185
              %li#DSJVR02
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keshav+Dasgupta"}> Keshav Dasgupta
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mohammad+Sheikh-Jabbari"} Mohammad Sheikh-Jabbari
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Van+Raamsdonk"} Mark Van Raamsdonk
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Matrix Perturbation Theory For M-theory On a PP-Wave
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205185"} arXiv:hep-th/0205185
            %p See also
            %ul
              %li#DuffInamiPopeSezginStelle88
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
                  , T. Inami,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Pope"} Christopher Pope
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Semiclassical Quantization of the Supermembrane
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/247064"} spire:247064
              %li#KabatTaylor97
                %p
                  Daniel Kabat,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Washington+Taylor"} Washington Taylor
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Spherical membranes in Matrix theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711078"} arXiv:hep-th/9711078
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Berkovits"}> Nathan Berkovits
                  ,
                  %em Towards Covariant Quantization of the Supermembrane
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201151"}> arXiv:hep-th/0201151
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  Qiang Jia,
                  %em On matrix description of D-branes
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.00142"}> arXiv:1907.00142
                  )
            %p
              A new kind of
